<!--ID=B7267351-473F-409D-9765-754A8EBCDE05;Version=1|{"VoiceNameToIdMapItems":[{"Id":"f1b99834-fbfc-4d32-846d-c4dbd3050c19","Name":"Microsoft Server Speech Text to Speech Voice (en-GB, OllieMultilingualNeural)","ShortName":"en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural","Locale":"en-GB","VoiceType":"StandardVoice"}]}-->
<!--ID=FCB40C2B-1F9F-4C26-B1A1-CF8E67BE07D1;Version=1|{"Files":{}}-->
<!--ID=5B95B1CC-2C7B-494F-B746-CF22A0E779B7;Version=1|{"Locales":{"en-US":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]},"en-GB":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]}}}-->
<speak xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis"
       xmlns:mstts="http://www.w3.org/2001/mstts"
       xmlns:emo="http://www.w3.org/2009/10/emotionml"
       version="1.0"
       xml:lang="en-GB">
  <voice name="en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural">
    <prosody rate="-11.50%" pitch="-2.90%">
            The shepherd arrives home.
            <break time="1800ms"/>
            And he does not quietly put the sheep back in the fold
            <break time="500ms"/>
            and say nothing about it.
            <break time="1800ms"/>
            He calls his friends and neighbors together.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            He calls for a gathering.
            <break time="1800ms"/>
            "Rejoice with me," he says.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            "For I have found my sheep that was lost."
            <break time="1800ms"/>
            He cannot keep the joy to himself.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            He has to share it with someone.
            <break time="1800ms"/>
            Think about that.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            One sheep.
            <break time="500ms"/>
            One ordinary animal.
            <break time="500ms"/>
            And its return is worth a celebration.
            <break time="1800ms"/>
            Not just a quiet relief that things worked out.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            Not a sigh and a note in the record.
            <break time="1800ms"/>
            A party.
            <break time="1800ms"/>
            The response to something lost being found
            <break time="500ms"/>
            is disproportionate joy.
            <break time="1800ms"/>
            This is the character of the shepherd Jesus is describing.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            He finds the one.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            He brings it home.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            And then he throws a party.
            <break time="1800ms"/>
            The celebration is not an afterthought.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            The celebration is the point.
            <break time="1000ms"/>
            Your return is worth celebrating.
    </prosody>
  </voice>
</speak>
